  "sentences": {
    "s1": "# AI Is the Star, but the Trailer Is for the Whole Company!",
    "s2": "The “Cast” of Numbers in Broadcom’s Earnings",
    "s3": "“AI semiconductor revenue: $16.7 billion!” If that number fills the screen, you hear a fanfare in your head.",
    "s4": "The star, AI, seems to have pulled off another big job.",
    "s5": "Then the words “Next: about $34.8 billion” appear.",
    "s6": "Wow, is the sequel suddenly going to be much bigger?",
    "s7": "Wait a minute.",
    "s8": "Has this edit joined two different numbers?",
    "s9": "Broadcom’s earnings report is much easier to follow if we check the “cast” of the numbers.",
    "s10": "Revenue for the company as a whole was $29.591 billion.",
    "s11": "That is the result for the whole company.",
    "s12": "By contrast, $16.7 billion was revenue from AI semiconductors.",
    "s13": "Even though both appear in the same announcement, they show different things—like a group photo of the entire cast and a close-up of the star.",
    "s14": "So what is about $34.8 billion?",
    "s15": "It is the company’s forecast for its total revenue in the next quarter.",
    "s16": "In other words, what is being previewed is the whole company next time, not the future of AI semiconductors alone.",
    "s17": "If a caption said, “AI revenue rises from $16.7 billion to $34.8 billion!”, that would not be the company’s announcement.",
    "s18": "It would be an overly bold re-edit by the audience.",
    "s19": "Now let’s sort out the cast list.",
    "s20": "$16.7 billion is “AI semiconductor results.” $29.591 billion is “whole-company results.” About $34.8 billion is “whole-company forecast.” “AI or the whole company?” and “Actual results or a forecast?” If we remove these two labels, the earnings report quickly turns into a comedy of mix-ups.",
    "s21": "Of course, AI does get its big moment.",
    "s22": "The CEO said that demand for custom AI accelerators and networking remains very strong.",
    "s23": "It is a strong line that gives a sense of the star’s momentum.",
    "s24": "We should listen to it as it is.",
    "s25": "But even if the company’s forecast appears beside that line, we cannot say, “AI demand is strong, so revenue will be about $34.8 billion.” This announcement alone does not explain how the two are connected.",
    "s26": "We should not see two scenes next to each other and make up the script in between.",
    "s27": "The key questions when looking at earnings are: “What is this number for?” and “Is it an actual result or a forecast?” Just these two questions are enough to clearly separate the star’s performance from the outlook for the whole production.",
    "s28": "AI deserves applause.",
    "s29": "But the sign for the next preview says “the whole company.” Let’s pause for a moment with the popcorn in hand and make sure we don’t miss that.",
    "s30": "## In one line",
    "s31": "Broadcom’s $34.8 billion forecast is for the whole company, not just AI semiconductors."
  },
  "facts": {
    "F1": "対象企業はBroadcom Inc.。同社は2026年9月2日、2026年度第3四半期の決算を発表した。\n  scope: Broadcom Inc.の連結業績\n  date_or_period: 2026年9月2日発表。2026年度第3四半期（2026年8月2日終了）\n  ambiguity_note: Broadcomが2026年9月2日に2026年度第3四半期（2026年8月2日終了）の決算を発表したことは確認できました。ただし、対象テーマの「最も最近の発表」という選定条件は、Broadcomの発表日だけでは確認できません。たとえば「leading AI chipmaker」にAI向けメモリのMicronも含めるなら、同社は9月30日にFY2026第4四半期の決算を発表しており、Broadcomより後です。分類の範囲が曖昧なため、Broadcomを選定対象とする前提は確定できません。([investors.broadcom.com](https://investors.broadcom.com/news-releases/news-release-details/broadcom-inc-announces-third-quarter-fiscal-year-2026-financial))",
    "F2": "Broadcomの第3四半期の純売上高は295億9,100万ドルだった。\n  scope: Broadcom Inc.全体の四半期純売上高\n  conditions: 決算リリースの財務ハイライトでは金額を百万ドル単位で表示。\n  numeric_value: 29,591百万ドル（295億9,100万ドル） (numeric_scope: 連結純売上高)\n  date_or_period: 2026年度第3四半期（2026年8月2日終了）",
    "F3": "Broadcomの第3四半期のAI半導体売上高は167億ドル。CEOは前年同期比221％増、前四半期比54％増と説明した。\n  scope: AI半導体売上高。Broadcom全体の純売上高や半導体部門全体とは別の数値。\n  conditions: 金額はCEO発言で10億ドル単位に丸めて示された。\n  numeric_value: 167億ドル。前年同期比+221％、前四半期比+54％。 (numeric_scope: 同四半期のAI半導体売上高と、その前年同期・前四半期比)\n  date_or_period: 2026年度第3四半期（2026年8月2日終了）\n  causal_strength: OBSERVED_REPORTED\n  notes_for_writer: 「AI半導体売上高」と記し、半導体ソリューション部門全体の売上高と混同しない。",
    "F4": "Broadcomは次の四半期の連結売上高を約348億ドルと見込んだ。同社は前年比93％増に相当すると説明した。\n  scope: Broadcom Inc.全体の次四半期連結売上高\n  conditions: 2026年9月2日時点の会社見通し。会社は見通しを推定値とし、実績は異なり、差が重要となる可能性があると記載。\n  numeric_value: 約348億ドル。前年同期比+93％。 (numeric_scope: 2026年度第4四半期の連結売上高見通しと前年同期比)\n  date_or_period: 2026年度第4四半期（2026年11月1日終了予定）\n  notes_for_writer: 会社の見通しとして記載し、確定した実績値として扱わない。",
    "F5": "BroadcomのCEOは、次の四半期のAI半導体売上高を217億ドルと見込み、前年同期比236％増になると述べた。\n  scope: BroadcomのAI半導体売上高。連結売上高見通しとは別の数値。\n  conditions: 会社CEOによる決算リリース時点の見通し。\n  numeric_value: 217億ドル。前年同期比+236％。 (numeric_scope: 2026年度第4四半期のAI半導体売上高見通しと前年同期比)\n  date_or_period: 2026年度第4四半期（2026年11月1日終了予定）\n  notes_for_writer: 会社の見通しとして記載し、実績値と混同しない。",
    "F6": "BroadcomのCEOは、カスタムAIアクセラレーターとネットワーキングへの需要が引き続き非常に強いと述べた。\n  scope: 同社のカスタムAIアクセラレーターおよびネットワーキングに対する需要についてのCEOの説明\n  conditions: 経営陣による定性的な評価。\n  date_or_period: 2026年9月2日発表の2026年度第3四半期決算リリース\n  causal_strength: OBSERVED_REPORTED\n  notes_for_writer: 会社CEOの評価として帰属を明記し、独立に確認された市場全体の需要事実として一般化しない。"
